comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T20:28:06.351Z",codex-agent,"Verified F10 and F11 against origin/main 8b8d693ea0808c8d49d1291ad94e9faeb1139ce5. F10 is valid: CommandError lacks the SDK discriminator and wrapCommandError preserves only local instances. F11 is valid: blocker-cuts manually scans numeric flags that are absent from registration. Plan: SDK factory/predicate/constants, typed command flags and normalized options; real no-git tracker, host harness, behavioural reverts, unchanged coverage gates. The pinned SDK already exposes the named exports; no dependency bump planned."
  "2026-10-23T20:32:20.108Z",codex-agent,"The host requires schema capability for registerCommand flags, so manifest.json and public harness capability declarations include it. Focused regressions and the linked pm test run passed 10/10 with no skips. F10 behavioural revert: restored only legacy error construction/wrapping, then node --test test/sdk-host-refusals.test.ts failed 3/3: conflict became CommandError exit 1 instead of the original PmCliError exit 4, usage failed isPmCliExpectedError, and the unexpected-error cause contract failed. Restored the implementation afterward."
  "2026-10-23T20:32:35.570Z",codex-agent,"F11 behavioural revert: restored only registerBlockerCuts registration/parsing to origin/main, rebuilt dist, then node --test test/blocker-cuts-command.test.ts failed 2/7 (5 passed): normalized options no longer validated, and the command contract lacked --max-states. The fixed command consumes host-normalized options; separated and equals forms produce identical cuts and receipts, and malformed values exit 2 before search. Restored source and rebuilt dist. SDK pin, peer minimum, manifest pm_min_version and all coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T20:41:24.214Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm gate exposed two legacy assertions coupled to F10: an explicit invalid tracker expected the local CommandError name, and the canonical graph-engine missing-tracker refusal expected flattening to exit 1. Updated them to assert isPmCliExpectedError and preserve native NOT_FOUND exit 3. Both targeted assertions now pass. All graph wrapping boundaries retain expected-error identity and unexpected causes. The published SDK at the existing advertised minimum 2026.10.13 includes all named helpers, confirming no dependency or minimum-version change is needed."
  "2026-10-23T20:56:17.112Z",codex-agent,The complete suite reached 99.72% lines / 96.09% branches / 100% functions at the original thresholds. Its only remaining failure was a Cypher test that expected an unhandled-error result; the command now correctly preserves a typed usage refusal. Updated that assertion and its targeted scenario passes. The full gates will be rerun with that final test expectation. Production code is unchanged after this suite run.
  "2026-10-23T21:10:15.821Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passed on the final production and test changes: 395/395 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos; 99.70% lines, 96.11% branches, 100% functions at unchanged thresholds. The gate used isolated HOME and Git configuration. The linked pm test run passed again: 10/10 focused regressions. Full bun run release:check is running on the same code. Changelog regeneration will follow the final tracker writes."
  "2026-10-23T21:15:48.387Z",codex-agent,"Full bun run release:check passed: 395/395 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos; 99.78% lines, 96.26% branches, 100% functions. Full npm release gate also passed 395/395 (99.70/96.11/100). Both used isolated HOME/Git settings and unchanged coverage thresholds. Linked regression run passed 10/10. Both behavioural revert proofs are recorded above. SDK pin and advertised minimum are unchanged, and no new PM CLI/SDK bug was encountered. Regenerate CHANGELOG.md after this final tracker write and claim release; keep this Task in progress for orchestrator verification. Next: commit code, generated text output and tracker evidence together, open the PR, and wait for CI; no merge or release."
